Z||000000||MooCow||11-22-2000||01:43 PM||||I have to do a paper on Web Designer's because that is the field I ma going into.<BR>If you dont mind I would like to ask you a few questions to help me out.   <BR> Do you work by yourself or for a company?<BR> Do you just make web sites for anyone that would like one?<BR> Do you keep updating the sites or not?<BR>I really just need to know the ups and down of this occupation.  <BR>I have started to amke a web page for my dad's company but have not yet taken any real HTML courses.  This winter I will be taking my first HTML class at Baker College.  Any sites on HTML would help me out greatly because I do know you can't use such programs as Front Page to make a proffesional Web site.<BR>Also let me know anything I should know about getting started in this field.<BR>Sorry for all the questions<BR>                                Thanks Ken<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-22-2000||02:43 PM||||Who told you you can't use front page for a commercial site? How useful FP and Office are depends on just what you are doing. It's used for allot of sites, espcially those running on MS IIS. FP and Office are very helpful tools if you know how to use them. (There are very few other programs with as huge a spell check dictionary as Word has.)<P>Where FP and Office have problems is in handeling some of the java stuff and certain other things. sometimes you have to hand install these problem children. once they are in the page the MS products usually are ok about it. It's just getting it added to begin with that's usually an issue.<P>As for the rest,,,, <P>No one but a complete loon does this or anything else professionally without being incorporated in one way or another. Working without that protection means you can loose all your personal things if someone sues you. Even then you can lose everything if you don't set up the inc/co/llc/whatever correctly.<P>How much you update depends on the site and your contract.<P>How you "select" a client is as much a personal preferance as anything else. You may not want to deal with political or adult sites for any amount of cash. You may not be able to do what they want. You don't like what they want.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-22-2000||04:30 PM||||<B>Do you work by yourself or for a company?</B><P>I have a registered business, with 2 employees..<P><B><BR> Do you just make web sites for anyone that would like one?</B><P>If they're a friend, sure.. but I charge clients.. heh<P><B> Do you keep updating the sites or not?<BR></B><P>if I'm asked to, yes..<P><B>I really just need to know the ups and down of this occupation.  <BR>I have started to amke a web page for my dad's company but have not yet taken any real HTML courses.  This winter I will be taking my first HTML class at Baker College.  Any sites on HTML would help me out greatly because I do know you can't use such programs as Front Page to make a proffesional Web site.</B><P>says who?? I use dreamweaver, and so does my friend Paul, who is the head web designer at Royal LePage (big real estate company) don't confuse a professioanl html creation tool with a cheap free one. writing html code by hand was ok a couple of years ago, but sites today are very complex, and it'd be next to impossible to not use an editor of some sort. I still edit the code by hand to tweak some stuff, but I mostly use the tools in dreamweaver.<P><B>Also let me know anything I should know about getting started in this field.</B><P>flex time. hehe.. best part..<P><B>Sorry for all the questions</B><P>questions are good.. it's a good way to learn.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you're interested in learning some graphics tricks too, check out my website. I have some free photoshop tutorials.. <P> <A HREF="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/stuff/tutorials/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/stuff/tutorials/</A> <P>as for Ogre's comments about being incorporated... I can't afford to do that, it's just a part time job for me.. I don't get enough business at present to warrant anything like that.. incorporating is expensive here.. about a grand, with legal fees.. possibly more.. I'm getting sick of all this legal crap, lawyers have made things too complicated. these days, if you smile at a girl and say hi to her... she can nail you for sexual harassment if she doesn't like you. it's ridiculous.. I've been screwed over many many times by clients, and I've never done anything.. but some people aren't as easy going, so if I ever did have a client that tried to sue me for something, I'd probably be SOL.... things were much simpler when I was a little kid.. *sigh*<P>sorry, that last bit wasn't too relevant to your questions.. but don't mind me, I'm just a loon..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000003||MooCow||11-23-2000||11:30 PM||||Thanks for all of the answer's.  So far this job sounds like fun.  Can't wait to finish my dad's company Web site.  I have been playing around with it for a long time but still can't figure out why some of the links and such dont work.<P>                           Thanks Ken||||reg||6
